      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T05:05:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is only called in AutomaticOnOffKeepaliveTracker#handleCheckKeepalivesStillValid. It sounds to me like a much better way of handling this would be to remove this method and move its implementation to the caller. You should be able to rewrite the loop over the `mAutomaticOnOffKeepalives` array in the same way :\n\n    for (final AutomaticOnOffKeepalive autoKi : mAutomaticOnOffKeepalives) {\n      final KeepaliveTracker.KeepaliveInfo ki \u003d autoKi.mKi;\n      if (!nai.equals(ki.mNai)) continue;\n        final int reason \u003d ki.isValid();\n        if (SUCCESS !\u003d reason) handleStopKeepalive(autoKi, reason);\n      }\n    }\n\nYou\u0027ll have to make `isValid` public but I think it\u0027s fine. You\u0027ll probably have to gather them in an array to stop them at the end like is done in this method (as opposed to my snippet) because handleStopKeepalive will mutate `mAutomaticOnOffKeepalives`\n\nThis will also let you remove a lot of the supporting methods you had to add to AutoOnOffKeepaliveTracker I think.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 619,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 619,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "1e0a2577644746b0b05569643140fd3a7f78082e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
