      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T05:05:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Moot if you implement my comment above, but suggestion : you can save some performance by checking emptiness first here, since this is called for each change of link properties but there are almost never invalid keepalives. It could look like :\n\n    if (invalidKeepalives.size() \u003d\u003d 0) return Collections.emptyList();\n    final ArrayList\u003cInteger\u003e invalidSlots \u003d new ArrayList\u003c\u003e();\n    for (Pair\u003cInteger, Integer\u003e slotAndError: invalidKeepalives) {\n      handleStopKeepalive(nai, slotAndError.first, slotAndError.second);\n      invalidSlots.add(slotAndError.first);\n    }\n    return invalidSlots;\n\nI appreciate the intention of making an unmodifiable list but in practice this comes from a locally-generated array so nothing bad can possibly come from modifying it, therefore the unmodifiable wrapper is pure overhead. If you want you can have a comment about that.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 628,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 628,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "1e0a2577644746b0b05569643140fd3a7f78082e",
