      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T05:05:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Something looks wrong ; if you exit through line 697 this calls KI#cleanup and then you return false, which calls AutoKI#cleanup. But if you exit through l.700, it\u0027s only AutoKI#cleanup.\n\nI think we should at least have a return in both branches to clarify that both cases have been considered appropriately, but returning the reason here is also useful to clarify what happens in AutoKI when this is not success.\n\nIn fact, there is also a more holistic way of arguing for this : in practice this method returns whether the autoKI should cleanup, when it should not know about it. That\u0027s another way to see why returning the reason is probably a better idea.",
